### Herd Path Notes

This project uses Laravel Herd for local development. If PHP commands fail, use the full Herd path:

| Tool     | Herd Path                                               |
| -------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |
| PHP      | `~/Library/Application Support/Herd/bin/php`            |
| Composer | `~/Library/Application Support/Herd/bin/composer`       |

**Example commands with Herd:**

```bash
PATH="$HOME/Library/Application Support/Herd/bin:$PATH" ~/Library/Application\ Support/Herd/bin/php ./vendor/bin/pint --dirty
PATH="$HOME/Library/Application Support/Herd/bin:$PATH" ~/Library/Application\ Support/Herd/bin/php artisan migrate --force
PATH="$HOME/Library/Application Support/Herd/bin:$PATH" ~/Library/Application\ Support/Herd/bin/composer install
```

### NPM Build with Herd

When running `npm run build`, the Vite Wayfinder plugin requires PHP to be in the PATH. If build fails with "php: command not found", prepend the Herd bin path to PATH:

```bash
PATH="$HOME/Library/Application Support/Herd/bin:$PATH" npm run build
PATH="$HOME/Library/Application Support/Herd/bin:$PATH" npm run build:ssr
```

This ensures Vite can find PHP when generating Wayfinder types during the build process.

